Prevent Payment on Newly Created Bills until Received
On Vendor Bill creation, WF/Script logic to check a custom field on the Bill called "Waiting Receipt Match" if the PO: Qty Received < PO: Qty Billed for at least 1 Bill Line
This checkbox would be used to hide the Make Payment button or otherwise prevent payment until matched to a Receipt
Release Held/Unmatched Bills after Item Receipt creation
This could maybe be a User Event script on Item Receipt creation, but probably Scheduled or Map/Reduce script (maybe scheduled every 30 minutes or 1 hour)
Script would look at Bills with "Waiting Receipt Match" = T for the PO that the newly or recently created Item Receipt(s) are linked to (linked via PO)
If {PO Qty Received} - {PO Qty Billed} >= 0 for all PO lines, Release all Held Bills for that PO
Script would calculate an "Unallocated Received Qty" for each PO Line that has a Bill "Waiting Receipt Match"
Unallocated Received Qty = PO Qty Received - (PO Qty Billed - Sum(Bill Qty of Held Bills))
*This allows you to separate the PO Qty Received that has already been allocated/matched to one or more previous Bills
If Unallocated Rec Qty >= 0, check If Bill Qty <= Unallocated Rec Qty on earliest Bill, Then release Hold. Proceed down the list of Held Bills, reducing Unallocated Rec Qty each time a Bill is release, until Unallocated Rec Qty < Bill Qty for at least 1 line of the Bill
